    "commentators": {
      "body": "On-the-ground Tesla commentators flooded X with Cybercab ride reports as paid service opened more widely in Austin. Sawyer Merritt said he logged about three hours in Cybercab for roughly $92.51\u2014versus an estimated $200 for comparable Uber trips\u2014and called FSD V15 free of major complaints after rides including a ~40-minute downtown-to-north Austin run. He also noted wait times jumping from minutes to over an hour once public demand spiked.\n\nFarzad previewed subscriber video asking whether Cybercab can displace Uber and said he hopes Tesla reaches the safety validation needed to drop thousands of units in Austin and expand the geofence far enough to hail from home. Separately he continued covering AI infrastructure topics such as advanced-node chip lithography and U.S. data-center build economics.\n\nWhole Mars Catalog posted a stream of Austin cabin impressions\u2014with Sawyer Merritt among ride companions\u2014praising legroom and the absence of a dividing console, highlighting the Robotaxi app as a primary control surface for vents, seats, ambient light, and Grok, and joking that a Model Y screen feels tiny after Cybercab\u2019s 22-inch display.",
